WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.029
“What about this one?” one SCP researcher
called to the other.

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:09.139
“You’ve got to be kidding,” his colleague
scoffed, interpreting the suggestion as little

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:10.139
more than a joke.

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:11.830
“That thing’s a piece of junk.”

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.850
She tapped a knuckle against the glass case,
catching the attention of the tiny figure

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.850
inside.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.850
“Who dares?”

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.539
exclaimed a tinny, monotone voice.

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:25.510
“Release me from this irksome confinement
so that I may bring about your final undoing,

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:26.510
vermin!

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:30.830
For I am DoomBot 2000, the ultimate bringer
of destruction.”

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.540
Both researchers laughed at the small automaton
inside the glass.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:41.120
They had come to SCP Item Gallery 27 in search
of non-organic anomalies to gather for testing,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.989
but judging by their reactions, it seemed
that SCP-1370 wasn’t going to make the cut.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:51.620
The cobbled-together robot was widely considered
to be a harmless, clumsy little oddity, rather

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.210
than any kind of threat.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:59.530
But that didn’t stop SCP-1370 from challenging
any and all things around it to a battle to

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.670
the death.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.340
Battles it always lost.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.280
“This thing is junk,” the second researcher
remarked, flicking her finger at the glass

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.980
again in an attempt to startle the robot.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:15.530
“It’s not organic, though,” the other
pointed out, observing that SCP-1370 had been

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:18.259
constructed out of various recycled parts.

00:01:18.259 --> 00:01:23.290
Its head was a defunct and non-operational
voltmeter, soldered awkwardly onto a weak

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.439
neck joint.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:30.579
Its arms were wrenches, and it had been configured
in such a way that gave the robot a top-heavy,

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:31.790
impractical design.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.830
“Inorganic, yes, but worth our time?

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:35.830
Definitely not.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:39.240
Come on, we’ll find something else to test
in SCP-914.”

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.540
As the pair of researchers turned their backs
on SCP-1370, it began to squawk at them again

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.090
through the speaker embedded in its chest.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.890
“You dare walk away from me?

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:53.150
You have incurred the wrath of RoboLord the
Destructor, and will soon be reduced to atoms

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.680
by my hand!”

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:00.020
The tiny junk robot charged towards the two
Foundation personnel, only to slam front-first

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.500
into the glass of the display case it was
kept contained in.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:09.140
The force of the impact, combined with SCP-1370’s
imbalanced design, caused it to topple over

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.040
and land on its back, leaving a huge crack
in the glass.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.640
“Oh great,” one of the researchers sighed,
rolling her eyes.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.030
“We’re going to have to report that SCP-1370’s
damaged its case again.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.170
Come on, let’s go and get someone to replace
that glass.”

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:28.670
“You think we should just leave it here
unsupervised in a damaged case?” the other

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.670
asked.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.950
“Look at the thing, it’s hardly competent
enough to escape,” the fellow researcher

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.319
replied, as the tiny robot struggled to get
itself back upright.

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:40.390
“I’m sure it’ll be fine for a few minutes.”

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:46.550
Little did the pair of researchers realize
as they left Item Gallery 27, that SCP-1370

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:51.160
had been listening to their conversation,
picking up on a few details.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:55.280
While the anomalous automaton often displayed
a low level of intelligence and awareness

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.030
of its surroundings, it was still self-aware.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:04.519
And on top of that, harbored a hatred for
all things it believed to be living; although

00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:09.409
it could easily be tricked, and lacked any
kind of real fighting ability.

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:15.580
But it had picked up on something the researchers
had mentioned, an ‘SCP-914’.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:20.819
Perhaps through its own limited intelligence
or some other kind of anomalous awareness,

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:24.970
the tiny robot detected this to mean another
machine.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:29.790
And so, standing back up, it struck the glass
of its display case again, shattering one

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.540
side completely.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.010
It hopped down to the ground, tumbling over
thanks to its lack of balance, only to eventually

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.170
stand back up and start making its way through
the facility.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:46.390
Being only a meter tall made it easy for SCP-1370
– otherwise known as ‘PesterBot’ – to

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.459
sneak through the corridors of the Foundation
site undetected.

00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:55.080
It eventually arrived at a room housing a
large mass of gears and gyros, a machine filled

00:03:55.080 --> 00:04:00.450
with clockwork components that seemed to pull
the little robot further in as it drew closer

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.409
and closer to what the researchers had spoken
of.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:10.000
SCP-914, the Clockworks, a device that could
be used to refine any object placed inside

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.000
it.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.470
Depending on the setting, items could be transformed,
destroyed, or vastly improved using the Clockworks.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:21.169
‘Rough’ setting disintegrated any test
subject, while ‘Coarse’ dismantled it

00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:22.880
to its base components.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.270
‘1:1’ replaced any item with an almost
identical copy.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:32.160
Then, the ‘Fine’ setting would cause SCP-914
to improve any item, and ‘Very Fine’ could

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:38.440
refine an object to an even greater degree,
usually by granting it anomalous properties.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:43.810
Testing of all biological matter within SCP-914
was strictly prohibited, but PesterBot…

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:46.980
well, he was made of metal.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:52.330
Sneaking into the room where the Clockworks
was located, SCP-1370 immediately caught sight

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:56.820
of another Foundation researcher, who had
been busy overseeing tests using the Very

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:59.340
Fine setting of SCP-914.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:04.190
Instantly, the agitated little robot made
a beeline for the researcher, swiping at her

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.840
ankles with its wrench hands.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:06.840
“Die, die!”

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:07.960
it shrieked.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:13.350
“Cower before the might of my claws, none
can stand before the relentless destruction

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:16.530
brought forth by ShivaTron, Despoiler of Mirth!”

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:21.169
referring to itself with one of its many elaborate,
self-appointed titles.

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:25.660
Caught by surprise at the tiny robot, the
researcher turned and screamed in surprise.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:30.080
Instinctively, she swung her leg back and
brought it forward, delivering a swift kick

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:36.699
to SCP-1370 that sent its metal body hurtling
through the air… right into the Clockworks.

00:05:36.699 --> 00:05:41.560
PesterBot landed inside the ‘Input’ booth,
the enormous collection of clockwork components

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.690
whirring and heaving as they sprung to life.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.280
The researcher hadn’t even realized what
was happening.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.190
She’d been addressing how much her foot
hurt after kicking the small metal robot.

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:58.910
By the time she looked up, SCP-914 had already
fully activated with SCP-1370 inside.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:04.580
In horror, she sounded the alarm to summon
security, with no idea what the ‘Very Fine’

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:08.001
setting would do to improve the PesterBot.

00:06:08.001 --> 00:06:11.970
A team of guards filed into the room, drawing
their weapons and training them on the Output

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.729
booth of the Clockworks.

00:06:13.729 --> 00:06:18.630
While they normally would have nothing to
fear from SCP-1370, given its inability to

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.470
ever win a fight that it started.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:26.039
Even when fighting a potted plant that had
been affixed with a speaker, the tiny robot

00:06:26.039 --> 00:06:27.039
had been bested.

00:06:27.039 --> 00:06:31.509
But the Clockworks refinement process meant
that what would be stepping out of the machine

00:06:31.509 --> 00:06:36.360
wouldn’t be the PesterBot the Foundation
was familiar with.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:41.000
Sure enough, the heavy foot that came stomping
down on the facility floor was a far cry from

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.010
the flimsy metal limbs SCP-1370 had previously
had.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:51.520
Out of the Clockworks emerged a hulking robotic
form, not just bigger and bulkier than the

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:57.449
meter tall, clumsily assembled PesterBot,
but a huge, sleek machine built for bear.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:01.550
It was more humanoid, but stood at nearly
seven feet tall.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:06.169
The weight imbalance issued that had plagued
the previous design were seemingly gone, as,

00:07:06.169 --> 00:07:12.810
despite its increased size, this new and improved
model of SCP-1370 seemed to move fluidly,

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:15.479
with smooth, electronic motions.

00:07:15.479 --> 00:07:19.949
The robot turned and assessed its surroundings,
scanning the group of Foundation security

00:07:19.949 --> 00:07:25.669
that had amassed outside SCP-914: its first
new targets.

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:30.860
As the machine stepped towards them, the security
commander gave the word, and the guards opened

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:31.860
fire.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:36.539
A hail of gunfire rang out, deafening shots
ringing in the security officers’ ears as

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:40.530
bullets spat out of their weapons toward the
newly refined PesterBot.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:44.560
By the time each of them had emptied their
magazines, and the smoke cleared, they realized

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.270
to their terror, that the robot was now bulletproof.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:53.830
“You have engaged in an act of violence
against Doom-Master Thirteen Seventy, Master

00:07:53.830 --> 00:08:00.410
of All Doom,” it announced in a new voice,
one far deeper and more imposing than its

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:07.330
previous tinny candor; now it was a modulated,
electronic sound, far befitting its new look.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:10.729
“Prepare to face consequences.

00:08:10.729 --> 00:08:12.030
Retaliating.”

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:16.970
With that, the robot leaped into battle with
all the grace and ferocity of a wild cat.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:21.090
The nearest security guard barely had a chance
to reload his weapon, raising his hands in

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:25.789
a weak attempt at a block before the strike
from a metallic fist knocked the wind out

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:26.789
of him.

00:08:26.789 --> 00:08:31.449
Moving with balletic speed and precision,
the PesterBot swiped and chopped at the guard,

00:08:31.449 --> 00:08:35.570
each hit connecting painfully with one of
the man’s vital pressure points, like it

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.729
was a highly trained hand-to-hand fighter.

00:08:38.729 --> 00:08:43.000
When the officer collapsed, unable to move
save for letting out screams of excruciating

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.780
pain, the robot turned to face its remaining
targets.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:47.780
“Freeze!”

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:52.209
one of the Foundation security yelled, raising
his pistol with shaking hands.

00:08:52.209 --> 00:08:57.320
Zipping forwards, SCP-1370 grabbed the gun
and wrenched it from the man’s fingers,

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:00.440
tearing the weapon apart like it was made
of cardboard.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:05.880
Gripping the man by his SCP Foundation uniform,
it launched him directly upwards, sending

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.290
his body crashing through the ceiling, leaving
a human-shaped hole above.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:15.029
Chunks of building materials rained down on
the robot, including wiring, and internal

00:09:15.029 --> 00:09:19.540
lengths of cable that ran through the walls
and ceiling that were now exposed.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:25.100
As the security team retreated, SCP-1370 curiously
reached up and gripped one of the electric

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:30.300
cables, wrenching it out of the ceiling to
examine it closer, causing sparks to shower.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:35.339
The PesterBot’s new sleek, metallic skin
seemed to react to the metal in the wiring,

00:09:35.339 --> 00:09:39.630
drawing out the copper that channeled electricity
throughout the Foundation facility.

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:44.190
It was more than a force of magnetism, it
was something else…

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:51.380
ideas, SCP-1370 was learning, adapting, and
most frighteningly of all, coming up with

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:54.410
new ways to complete its purpose.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:58.690
Marching up to the nearest wall, it pulled
back a metal fist and sent it slamming through

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:04.079
paintwork and plaster, to draw out the metal
running through the building.

00:10:04.079 --> 00:10:06.260
Outside in the corridor, the lights died.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:11.589
In fact, the entire facility lost its power,
and plunged into darkness until the backup

00:10:11.589 --> 00:10:16.570
emergency lighting activated, filling the
Foundation’s corridors with low-level, blood-red

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:17.570
light.

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:22.790
More security officers had mobilized to outside
the Clockworks room, expecting any moment

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:27.950
that the refined version of the previously
harmless PesterBot would soon appear.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:33.470
Sure enough, it did, and the red lighting
was soon added to by yet another hail of frightened

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:34.470
gunfire.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:40.480
But now, it seemed SCP-1370 had learned how
to shoot back.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:45.210
An arc of lightning zapped through the corridor,
electrifying every guard it touched and reducing

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:47.590
them to little more than a smoldering husk.

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:52.810
A second one followed, striking one guard
with a bolt of blue electricity that then

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:56.860
leaped from his body to the officer standing
next to him, who had been close enough to

00:10:56.860 --> 00:11:01.660
touch his fallen comrade, and who was, of
course, wearing plenty of conductive metal.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:08.850
The wiring in the walls, the electricity,
SCP-1370 had learned how to weaponize it.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.850
And that wasn’t all.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:15.110
As the robot stepped out of the room, it had
pulled various other metalwork from the fabric

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:21.360
of the building around it into its form, adding
to its body in new and gruesome ways.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:26.450
Its shoulders now had additional armor; long
poles of rebar now extended out of its robotic

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:32.710
forearms to act as crude, rudimentary impaling
weapons – it had even gotten taller.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:36.310
And all forged out of metal it had harvested
from its surroundings.

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:41.610
SCP-1370 hadn’t just been made a better
fighter, it had been given something else

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.570
by SCP-914.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:48.700
Intelligence, the capacity for it to learn
and perpetually adapt itself.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:54.860
And it wouldn’t stop, it would keep improving
itself to enact its original purpose: to fight

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:57.810
anything and everything around it.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:03.079
A slaughter ensued, everything the SCP Foundation
threw at this new version of the PesterBot

00:12:03.079 --> 00:12:08.500
only gave it more weapons, and more offensive
capabilities to add to its growing arsenal.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:13.760
The rebar weapons in its arms were replaced
with sleek, sharp blades, even bullets fired

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:18.870
at it seemed to be absorbed into its mass,
allowing it to keep growing.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:25.900
SCP-1370 was unstoppable, obliterating everyone
that came to desperately try to contain it.

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:31.230
And as it bested every opponent, left them
decimated and defeated, something else new

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.000
happened to the robot.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.230
It couldn’t feel emotions, just like with
any automaton, it lacked the level of human

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:41.200
cognition and complexity to respond to things
with feelings.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:45.850
But as it killed more and more Foundation
staff left and right, annihilating everything

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:50.750
in its path, SCP-1370 experienced something.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:56.970
Not an emotion, but whatever the closest robotic
equivalent to pure, unbridled happiness was.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:03.380
Satisfaction of the machine, now able to complete
the function it was originally built for,

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.020
yet had failed at for so long.

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:12.360
Getting bigger and bigger, adapting and adding
more machines to itself, eventually SCP-1370

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:13.630
was a hulking behemoth.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:19.139
Cars, and their combustion engines all became
part of the robotic giant, every new piece

00:13:19.139 --> 00:13:22.779
of technology it encountered becoming a deadly
weapon.

00:13:22.779 --> 00:13:28.490
And as PesterBot started to tower over buildings,
a huge-scale robotic threat, the Foundation

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.130
had no choice.

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:36.870
It was time to deploy another big, bad bot
to cut SCP-1370 back down to size.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:40.460
It was time to send in the Dragonslayer.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:46.889
Now go check out “WHAT IF SCP-096 WAS PUT
INSIDE SCP-914?”, where the Shy Guy is refined

00:13:46.889 --> 00:13:47.889
into…

00:13:47.889 --> 00:13:49.459
well, you’ll have to click and see!

00:13:49.459 --> 00:13:54.170
And “SCP-914 WHAT DID YOU PUT IN IT?!”
to see what happened when we opened up the

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:56.610
Clockworks to you, the fans!

